TA: Cold War espionage.

01:18:00.600 --> 01:18:02.560
And the internet.

01:18:15.480 --> 01:18:16.730
AUDIENCE: Communism.

01:18:28.130 --> 01:18:29.380
AUDIENCE: Computer virus.

01:18:48.408 --> 01:18:49.658
AUDIENCE: Hurricanes
and oceans.

01:19:01.310 --> 01:19:02.720
AUDIENCE: Could you do something
like astrology,

01:19:02.720 --> 01:19:05.000
which is not a real-world
system, but is--

01:19:05.000 --> 01:19:07.170
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

01:19:07.170 --> 01:19:07.506
TA: Yes.

01:19:07.506 --> 01:19:09.570
You can do astrology.

01:19:09.570 --> 01:19:10.840
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

01:19:10.840 --> 01:19:12.300
virus.

01:19:12.300 --> 01:19:13.340
AUDIENCE: Yeah.

01:19:13.340 --> 01:19:16.120
But that would be more
like a real virus.

01:19:19.390 --> 01:19:23.920
TA: I would suggest limiting
yourselves to

01:19:23.920 --> 01:19:24.880
just the real world.

01:19:24.880 --> 01:19:27.910
I mean, coming up with things
like zombie outbreaks, sure

01:19:27.910 --> 01:19:30.250
there is a system
you can model.

01:19:30.250 --> 01:19:34.640
But if you're just trying to
push on the edges of the

01:19:34.640 --> 01:19:38.570
constraints, then you're just
trying to give yourself an

01:19:38.570 --> 01:19:39.290
easier time.

01:19:39.290 --> 01:19:43.133
And more often I see the results
actually turn out to

01:19:43.133 --> 01:19:44.250
be less interesting because
people are just

01:19:44.250 --> 01:19:45.910
going for the ideas.

01:19:45.910 --> 01:19:47.260
They just [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

01:19:47.260 --> 01:19:48.505
them really, really quickly.

01:19:48.505 --> 01:19:51.730
People aren't actually
trying to work it.

01:19:51.730 --> 01:19:54.820
But that being said, even with
a lot of the ideas up here, a

01:19:54.820 --> 01:19:59.180
lot of them have connections.

01:19:59.180 --> 01:20:01.896
Even there will be
the obvious ones.

01:20:01.896 --> 01:20:04.884
Like oil spill containing and
oil spill starting could

01:20:04.884 --> 01:20:06.520
practically be the same thing.

01:20:06.520 --> 01:20:12.210
Everything with the presidential
election.

01:20:12.210 --> 01:20:14.150
Spreading mass hysteria
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

01:20:18.310 --> 01:20:21.834
And these ideas are now
up on the board.

01:20:21.834 --> 01:20:25.940
You have until the end
of Friday, I guess.

01:20:25.940 --> 01:20:28.210
We don't really need
to know until the

01:20:28.210 --> 01:20:29.500
beginning of next week.

01:20:29.500 --> 01:20:34.492
So actually by the end of
Friday, you should know who is

01:20:34.492 --> 01:20:38.960
on your team and what project
you're working on.

01:20:38.960 --> 01:20:42.580
Over the weekend, you know
who's on your team.

01:20:42.580 --> 01:20:45.070
You know to email people
on your team.

01:20:47.580 --> 01:20:49.440
And what idea you're
starting with.

01:20:49.440 --> 01:20:52.510
Again, the idea can diverge a
little bit, but I like the

01:20:52.510 --> 01:20:53.820
previous project.

01:20:53.820 --> 01:20:56.960
We do want you to keep with
whatever you started with and

01:20:56.960 --> 01:20:58.100
use it as core system.

01:20:58.100 --> 01:21:00.400
You may choose presidential
election.

01:21:00.400 --> 01:21:02.670
It may be something about
winning votes.

01:21:02.670 --> 01:21:05.085
And then you decide no, you
want to make a game of

01:21:05.085 --> 01:21:06.240
gerrymandering.

01:21:06.240 --> 01:21:07.580
That's fine.

01:21:07.580 --> 01:21:09.427
Because it's still keeping
in with the

01:21:09.427 --> 01:21:11.200
same core of the system.

01:21:11.200 --> 01:21:14.016
But say oh, we want to do
something about winning votes

01:21:14.016 --> 01:21:16.630
and then instead it became
about religion or

01:21:16.630 --> 01:21:17.510
something like that.

01:21:17.510 --> 01:21:20.042
I could see how you got there,
but that's not really keeping

01:21:20.042 --> 01:21:23.380
with the spirit at this
particular time.

01:21:23.380 --> 01:21:26.558
So stick with the original
core system that you're

01:21:26.558 --> 01:21:28.350
working with.

01:21:28.350 --> 01:21:29.990
And try to find the fun in it.

01:21:29.990 --> 01:21:32.520
Don't try to like, oh, this
is a really dull simulator

01:21:32.520 --> 01:21:34.413
mechanic, but if we add a bunch
of [UNINTELLIGIBLE] then

01:21:34.413 --> 01:21:35.260
it becomes funny.

01:21:35.260 --> 01:21:35.830
No.

01:21:35.830 --> 01:21:37.690
Try to find it fun in
the original system.

01:21:37.690 --> 01:21:40.860
And if you can't try to pick
apart the system and find the

01:21:40.860 --> 01:21:42.490
one component that is fun.

01:21:42.490 --> 01:21:46.605
So all of bomb making might
not be so much fun as as

01:21:46.605 --> 01:21:47.170
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

01:21:47.170 --> 01:21:47.740
the blood--

01:21:47.740 --> 01:21:50.060
Yeah, that might be
the fun part.

01:21:50.060 --> 01:21:53.350
The one part, I'll be, oops my
hand slipped, and therefore I

01:21:53.350 --> 01:21:54.550
am now dead.

01:21:54.550 --> 01:21:56.950
That part might be actually kind
of fun, as opposed to OK,

01:21:56.950 --> 01:21:58.390
now I need to figure out how
to get [UNINTELLIGIBLE].

01:22:02.710 --> 01:22:03.670
Cool.

01:22:03.670 --> 01:22:04.290
All these ideas are going
to stay up on

01:22:04.290 --> 01:22:05.540
the board for a while.